issue(1,'correctness','Density-limit entropy remainder is too strong','moderate','computation-error','chapters/13_scaling_phases.tex',r'nH_2(p)+O(\log n),','Only k(n)/n→p is assumed. For p=1/4 and k=floor(n/4+sqrt(n)), differentiability of entropy gives nH(k/n)-nH(p)=log2(3)*sqrt(n)+O(1), exceeding logarithmic error. The exponential classification survives.','Use nH2(k(n)/n)+O(log n)=nH2(p)+o(n), with the uniform Stirling argument.')
